  "note": "Triennial election, January 1932; counted in the Town Hall on Saturday 16 January by H. Sewell, town clerk and returning officer. Twenty candidates were nominated, including twelve retiring members (Northern Whig, 6 January 1932, p. 3); after three withdrawals (T. Hewitt, R. Courtney, sen., and G. A. Hyde) the North and South-East wards were contested. About 80 per cent of the North Ward electors voted and 60 per cent in the South-East. Party labels are not printed. South-West Ward: \"The following were returned unopposed\". (The Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1932, p. 7, says the North and South-West would be contested; the local report shows the South-West uncontested and the South-East polled.)"
